#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:22
msgid "Multi-parameter symbols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:24
msgid ""
"The :meth:`pygmt.Figure.plot` method can plot individual multi-parameter "
"symbols by passing the corresponding shortcuts (**e**, **j**, **r**, **R**, "
"**w**) to the ``style`` parameter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:28
msgid "**e**: ellipse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:29
msgid "**j**: rotated rectangle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:30
msgid "**r**: rectangle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:31
msgid "**R**: rounded rectangle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:32
msgid "**w**: pie wedge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:36
msgid ""
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Axis, Frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:44
msgid ""
"We can plot multi-parameter symbols using the same symbol style. We need to "
"define locations (lon, lat) via the ``x`` and ``y`` parameters (scalar for a "
"single symbol or 1-D list for several ones) and two or three symbol "
"parameters after those shortcuts via the ``style`` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:49
msgid "The multi-parameter symbols in the ``style`` parameter are defined as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:51
msgid "**e**: ellipse, ``direction/major_axis/minor_axis``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:52
msgid "**j**: rotated rectangle, ``direction/width/height``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:53
msgid "**r**: rectangle, ``width/height``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:54
msgid "**R**: rounded rectangle, ``width/height/radius``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:55
msgid ""
"**w**: pie wedge, ``diameter/startdir/stopdir``, the last two arguments are "
"directions given in degrees counter-clockwise from horizontal. Append **+i** "
"and the desired value to apply an inner diameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:59
msgid ""
"Uppercase versions **E**, **J**, and **W** are similar to **e**, **j**, and "
"**w** but expect geographic azimuths and distances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:64
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(region=[0, 7, 0, 2], projection=\"x3c\", frame=True)\n"
"\n"
"# Ellipse\n"
"fig.plot(x=0.5, y=1, style=\"e45/3/1\", fill=\"orange\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"# Rotated rectangle\n"
"fig.plot(x=1.5, y=1, style=\"j120/5/0.5\", fill=\"red3\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"# Rectangle\n"
"fig.plot(x=3, y=1, style=\"r4/1.5\", fill=\"dodgerblue\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"# Rounded rectangle\n"
"fig.plot(x=4.5, y=1, style=\"R1.25/4/0.5\", fill=\"seagreen\", pen=\"2p,"
"black\")\n"
"# Pie wedge\n"
"fig.plot(x=5.5, y=1, style=\"w2.5/45/330\", fill=\"lightgray\", pen=\"2p,"
"black\")\n"
"# Ring sector\n"
"fig.plot(x=6.5, y=1, style=\"w2.5/45/330+i1\", fill=\"lightgray\", pen=\"2p,"
"black\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:88
msgid ""
"We can also plot symbols with varying parameters via defining those values "
"in a 2-D list or numpy array (``[[parameters]]`` for a single symbol or "
"``[[parameters_1],[parameters_2],[parameters_i]]`` for several ones) or "
"using an appropriately formatted input file and passing it to ``data``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:93
msgid "The symbol parameters in the 2-D list or numpy array are defined as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:95
msgid "**e**: ellipse, ``[[lon, lat, direction, major_axis, minor_axis]]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:96
msgid "**j**: rotated rectangle, ``[[lon, lat, direction, width, height]]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:97
msgid "**r**: rectangle, ``[[lon, lat, width, height]]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:98
msgid "**R**: rounded rectangle, ``[[lon, lat, width, height, radius]]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:99
msgid ""
"**w**: pie wedge, ``[[lon, lat, diameter, startdir, stopdir]]``, the last "
"two arguments are directions given in degrees counter-clockwise from "
"horizontal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gallery/symbols/multi_parameter_symbols.rst:104
msgid ""
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"fig.basemap(\n"
"    region=[0, 7, 0, 4],\n"
"    projection=\"x3c\",\n"
"    frame=Frame(xaxis=Axis(annot=1, tick=0.2), yaxis=Axis(annot=0.5, "
"tick=0.1)),\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"# Ellipse\n"
"data = [[0.5, 1, 45, 3, 1], [0.5, 3, 135, 2, 1]]\n"
"fig.plot(data=data, style=\"e\", fill=\"orange\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"# Rotated rectangle\n"
"data = [[1.5, 1, 120, 5, 0.5], [1.5, 3, 50, 3, 0.5]]\n"
"fig.plot(data=data, style=\"j\", fill=\"red3\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"# Rectangle\n"
"data = [[3, 1, 4, 1.5], [3, 3, 3, 1.5]]\n"
"fig.plot(data=data, style=\"r\", fill=\"dodgerblue\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"# Rounded rectangle\n"
"data = [[4.5, 1, 1.25, 4, 0.5], [4.5, 3, 1.25, 2.0, 0.2]]\n"
"fig.plot(data=data, style=\"R\", fill=\"seagreen\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"# Pie wedge\n"
"data = [[5.5, 1, 2.5, 45, 330], [5.5, 3, 1.5, 60, 300]]\n"
"fig.plot(data=data, style=\"w\", fill=\"lightgray\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"# Ring sector\n"
"data = [[6.5, 1, 2.5, 45, 330], [6.5, 3, 1.5, 60, 300]]\n"
"fig.plot(data=data, style=\"w+i1\", fill=\"lightgray\", pen=\"2p,black\")\n"
"\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

